Kilobyte: where the source code is
==================================

Kilobyte's own programs (everything in /usr/lib/kilobyte, /usr/bin/kilobyte,
/usr/share/kilobyte and the other files it adds) are free software under the
GNU General Public License, version 3 or later (/usr/share/kilobyte/COPYING).
They are their own source code; the project is at
  https://github.com/jgm240/kilobyte

Everything else in this system comes from other free software projects, each
under its own licence (/usr/share/doc/*/copyright):

  Debian packages   source-packages.txt (next to this file) lists the source
                    package and the exact version of every package in this
                    image when it was made. The source of each one:
                      apt-get source PACKAGE=VERSION
                    or https://snapshot.debian.org/package/PACKAGE/VERSION/
  Kilobyte's own builds of dialog and ELinks (version "+kilobyte"):
                    Debian's source plus the changes in image/debs/ of the
                    Kilobyte repository.
  box86 (Raspberry Pi, 32-bit)
                    https://github.com/ptitSeb/box86 (MIT licence), the tag
                    named in its package version.
  yt-dlp            https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp (Unlicense), in
                    /usr/local/bin/yt-dlp; it is itself a Python program.
  Raspberry Pi kernel and firmware (Raspberry Pi images)
                    https://archive.raspberrypi.com/debian/ (apt-get source)
                    and https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux

Each release of Kilobyte on GitHub names the commit it was built from
(/usr/share/kilobyte/commit); image/build-in-container.sh shows how.
